<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102377" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξί̆αρχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>commander of a corps</i> or
				<i>squadron</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχοι ἀπὸ τῶν νεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.67
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχοι τῶν τελέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.42
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. καὶ πεζῶν καὶ ἱππέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					8.1.10
				</span></i>
			; in the army of Alexander, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.9.6
			</span></i>; in Ptolemaic Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMich.Zen.</u>
				70.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξιάρχης</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>commander of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάξις</span> (<i><span class="en">
				128
			</span></i> men), <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				9.3
			</span></i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άρχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					10.2
				</span></i>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			= Lat. <i>centurio</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.24.1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Zos.
				3.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			=
			<i>tribunus militum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				5.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.5.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cam.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				5.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				2.20
			</span></i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άρχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				3.39
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			=
			<i>legatus legionis</i>, anachronism in <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				4.6
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άρχαι</span> codd.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>d.</b>
			=
			<i>ordinarius</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mag.</u>
				1.46
			</span></i>, <u>Gloss.</u>; also glossed by <i>manipularis</i>
			and <i>evocatus</i>, ib. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Athens, <i>commander of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάξις</span>, or <i>quota of
			infantry</i> furnished by a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλή</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				569
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				1172
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				353
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				30.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				4.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				54.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.169
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.334.13
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τ.] ἡγεῖται τῶν φυλετῶν καὶ
					λοχαγοὺς καθίστησιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					61.3
				</span></i>
			; applied to naval officers, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.6.29
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				35
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
